WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.660
So something as serious as the impeachment
of a sitting president really shouldn't depend

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.660
on yeah, on

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.660
public opinion.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.290
Um, there have been a two impeachments of
presidents, Andrew Johnson and Bill Clinton.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.340
Neither was ultimately convicted by the Senate,
but it's still really serious stuff.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.310
If impeachment is the right thing based on
the facts, both Republicans and Democrats

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:24.109
should do it regardless of party and regardless
of public opinion.

00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:27.359
Now that's idealism and it's not based in
reality.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:28.869
It's not the system that we have.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:33.900
Our elected officials are highly partisan
on what even is worthy of impeachment.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.090
Uh, they're also completely influenced by
what the public wants at any particular point

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.090
in time.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.020
And a really great example is to look at Richard
Nixon's resignation.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.730
Nixon resigned because he was going to get
impeached.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.210
He was going to get impeached because Democrats
and Republicans in his own party, we're going

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.600
to impeach him.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.970
And there was bipartisan impeachment support
in the House and Senate because there was

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.230
more and more public support from both sides
for impeachment.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.370
So that brings us to 2019.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:08.420
And in Donald Trump's case in 2019, Republicans,
at least for the time being, still don't want

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.690
to impeach Donald Trump.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.060
And Democrats do.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.110
But support among independent voters has doubled
since May or almost doubled.

